dtc: fix multiple definition of yylloc with -fno-common

Both dtc-parser and dtc-lexer define YYLTYPE yylloc.  GCC 10 and newer
default to -fno-common, so linking the host dtc fails with:

  multiple definition of `yylloc'

Keep the lexer definition and make the parser refer to it with extern.

Signed-off-by: jeep <jeep@local>

--- linux-3.4.110.orig/scripts/dtc/dtc-parser.y	2015-10-22 09:20:09.000000000 +0800
+++ linux-3.4.110/scripts/dtc/dtc-parser.y	2026-10-01 20:06:02.401476286 +0800
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 #include "dtc.h"
 #include "srcpos.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 
 extern int yylex(void);
 extern void print_error(char const *fmt, ...);
--- linux-3.4.110.orig/scripts/dtc/dtc-parser.tab.c_shipped	2015-10-22 09:20:09.000000000 +0800
+++ linux-3.4.110/scripts/dtc/dtc-parser.tab.c_shipped	2026-10-01 20:06:02.401642194 +0800
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 #include "dtc.h"
 #include "srcpos.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 
 extern int yylex(void);
 extern void print_error(char const *fmt, ...);
